@startuml
title MVP Deployment lifecycle and scope recovery
hide empty description
state "Awaiting Confirmation\nAWAITING_CONFIRMATION" as Awaiting
state "Queued\nQUEUED" as Queued
state "Running\nRUNNING" as Running
state "Submitted\nSUBMITTED" as Submitted
state "Failed\nFAILED" as Failed
[*] --> Awaiting : C2 valid input / persist immutable snapshot
Awaiting --> Awaiting : C3 changed plan / invalid input\nno job; review token if plan changed
Awaiting --> Queued : C3 client=stored=rebuilt fingerprint\natomic guard+job+record+steps
Queued --> Running : C4 claim once under exclusive host lock\natomic CLAIMED + first step RUNNING
Running --> Running : C5-C7 phase progress
Running --> Submitted : C9 publication acknowledged\natomic record+job success+guard release
Running --> Failed : C4/C10/C11 stale input, phase error\nor verified interruption
Submitted --> [*]
Failed --> [*]
note right of Failed
  Unknown external outcome retains scope RECOVERY_REQUIRED.
  C12 verifies resource/CD state and releases scope with audit.
  Old deployment stays FAILED; next attempt is a NEW deployment.
end note
note right of Running
  Job phase: INFRASTRUCTURE, CONFIGURATION, MANIFEST, PUBLISH.
  No automatic replay or CLAIMED lease reclaim.
  Three internal steps; no persisted CD_SYNCED/APPLICATION_READY.
end note
note right of Submitted
  Platform accepted desired-state delivery.
  Argo Sync/Health are separate read-only observations.
end note
@enduml
